  "summary": "In John 20:17–18, Mary Magdalene turns from grief at the tomb to tell the disciples that she has seen the risen Jesus. The scene gives her a direct role in carrying the news to the others; it does not provide a full biography or support later claims that merge her with other Gospel women.",
  "historical_context": "The directly relevant passage in this record is John 20:17–23, where Mary reports to the disciples that she has seen Jesus. The scene supplies a narrative role but does not give details about her earlier life, family, or social position.",
