  "literary_context": "John’s resurrection scene moves from Mary’s grief and mistaken recognition to Jesus speaking her name. She then goes to the disciples with the report, “I have seen the Lord.” That movement makes recognition the turning point and Mary the first person in this scene to announce what has happened.",
  "covenantal_significance": "John 20 uses Mary’s encounter to move the resurrection account from the empty tomb to testimony among the disciples. Her report is a narrative link between the risen Jesus and the community that will hear the news; the passage does not require a fuller biography to make that role clear.",
